package "hooks" {

  class useBoardVision <<app>>
  class useIntentOverlays <<app>>
  class useBoardInput <<app>>
  class useCombatOverlays <<app>>
  class useAutoDeploy <<app>>
  class deriveVisualFrame <<app>>
  class teamTintStyle <<app>>
  class ccDamageCuesFromBoard <<app>>
  class visibleKingDamageCues <<app>>
  class withCCFire <<app>>
  class liveMatchPhase <<app>>
  class pieceVisibleToViewer <<app>>
  class charonArmed <<app>> {
    queuedCharonSquares(queue, side?)
    charonTrailSquares(resolve)
    restingCharonSquares(resolve, U:)
  }

  note bottom of charonArmed
    Sole owner of "which Mecha shows Charon launchers".
    Launchers are the Mecha's **own** charonMissiles spend and
    follow that unit — arming, a queued strike, the squares it
    held mid-resolve, then its resting square until turn-open
    clears U:. Never "gas was used on this square": U: and the
    absorb squares drive the green special-used aura only.
  end note

}

package "geometry / local stores" {
  class tankModeStore <<db>>
  class boardGeom <<app>>
}

package "presentation/pieces (units)" {

  class units <<app>> {
    InlinePawn / InlineKnight / InlineMecha
    InlineRook / InlineQueen / InlineKing
    TwinBattery · ccFire
    geometry.ts — pivots, rest aims, AimPose
    teamColors.ts — swatches, PIECE_FRAME
  }

  note bottom of units
    Sits **below** presentation/animations: the same unit draws
    a resting square and a combat cue, so animations/ imports
    down into here and never the reverse.

    Rest pose == apps/chess/public/pieces/nerd/*.svg — same
    PIECE_FRAME nest, same main stroke, no aim normalize.
    Aiming applies that normalize as a CSS transform
    (`styles/unitPose.css` .sc-unit-pose) so a mover settles
    back to rest over SETTLE_MS **at touchdown**; the move wave
    holds the mover one SETTLE_MS past arrival so the unwind
    finishes before the overlay hands the square to PieceGlyph
    (a CSS transition cannot span that unmount).

    **Never tween a reflection** — it squashes through a paper-thin
    frame. The Hoverbike's aim factors as [side] · rotate(40 − r):
    an outer .sc-unit-side group snaps the mirror, only the inner
    .sc-unit-pose rotation tweens. MoveAnimation fixes the side once
    per L (from the move's file direction) so the elbow only
    rotates; the touchdown snap hides behind a landing squash.
    Travel ticks come from core ""move-timing.ts"".
  end note

}

package "app state (external)" {
  class MatchStore <<db>>
  class capabilitiesStore <<db>>
}

