note right of teamTintStyle
  **Whose colour is it?** VFX that paints the *unit's own* ordnance — a
  Hoverbike's deploy jet and frag boom, a Ship's laser, a mine wreck's boom —
  reads ""--team-tint"" (hex, for ""color-mix"") and ""--team-rgb"" (triplet, for
  ""rgba"") with the white swatch as the CSS fallback. Fire and smoke stay fire
  and smoke: the tank's fuel plume and the shared death ""boomFlash"" are not
  team colours.

  It must sit on the **cue element**, never a layer root — a phase-1 window
  plays both sides' shots at once, so one tint per layer paints black's
  ordnance blue. Custom properties inherit, so a cue's slot covers its
  descendants (the Ship's laser pulse rides its hull slot).
end note

note bottom of DeathAnimation
  **A mine death draws the mine.** The cue carries ""piece = n"" — the
  Hoverbike that laid it owns the colour, not the shape — so ""deathNode""
  branches on ""cue.mine"" first and renders ""DeathMine"" (SpiderMine's own
  coordinates, shard-wrapped for the ""dyingDrama"" scatter) plus the bike's
  frag boom in place. Before that branch a shot-out mine had no hull at all:
  it vanished behind the generic ""boomFlash"".
end note

note right of withCCFire
  **One CC, one hull.** ""visibleKingDamageCues"" drops the persistent fire slot
  for a king whose square an attack owns (""attackFrom"") or whose side is mid-move
  (""movingColors""), so the animating layer owes that king its fire:
  ""withCCFire"" copies ""damage"" + ""seed"" onto the ""AttackCue"" / ""MoveCue"".
  Skip either half and the CC reads full HP for the length of the cue — skip the
  gate instead and two hulls draw it, fire (z 35) over mover (z 30).
  Shared ""seed"" keeps the flame spots from jumping at the handoff.
end note

note bottom
  StarChessBoard + VisionStrategy · CombatOverlayRoot + CombatCueFrame.
  ""useBoardVision"" ships beside ""useIntentOverlays"" (""presentation/combat/hooks/"").
  Design history: strategy-starchess-board · composite-vfx-stack. Screen hosts: ""screen-entities.puml"" (this folder).
end note

@enduml
